            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0692" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg600"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.94/307h</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-01T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5175. War Industries Board is sending abroad a group in connection with
                    arrangements for the participation of that Board in the discussion of
                    inter-Allied organizations being formed in Paris and London. Personnel of this
                    mission comprises Mr. Leland L. Summers, member of the Board, who will act as
                    head of the mission, Mr. Chandler P. Anderson, counsel for the War Industries
                    Board on international matters, Mr. George N. Armsby, Mr. Albert M. Patterson,
                    Mr. Lincoln Hutchinson, Mr. John Hughes, Mr. Edward A. Pierce, Mr. Paul Mackall,
                    Mr. Frederick K. Mxon, Mr. Arthur D. Whiteside, Mr. Henry W. Boyd, Mr. Hubert H.
                    Brooker, Mr. Philio B. Gait and Mr. James Bernard Mahoney. This mission is only
                    for the purpose of exchanging views and final action as result of this exchange
                    is to be referred back here for any necessary decision.</p>
                <p>Please communicate this information to French Government and repeat to Embassy
                    London for its information and that of the British Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
